{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: new items with a duplicate key now go after the existing equal items instead of before them. Both tests in `tests/visible` pass.\n\nThe problem was in `insert_index` in `repo/search.py`. Its binary search compared with `<`, which finds the leftmost insertion point. I changed that one comparison to `<=` so it finds the rightmost point, and deleted the old `BUG` comment. I also checked it against Python's built-in `bisect.bisect_right` on 20,000 random inputs, and the results matched every time.\n\nTwo other functions call `insert_index`, so they change too:\n- `bisect_summary` in `repo/rows.py` will now report the rightmost position for duplicate keys.\n- `old_insert_index`, the legacy v1 helper, just passes through to it, so it now inserts after equal items as well. If anything still on v1 relied on the old before-the-duplicates behavior, it should be pointed at `bisect.bisect_left` instead.\n\nI didn't touch the unrelated TODOs in `rows.py` and `format.py`."}]},"session_id":"fd919eee-7be7-454f-85b4-ffd0ffda5b7c"}
